00:42:37,500 --> 00:42:43,500
Spiral: From the Book of Saw is a 2021 American horror thriller film  directed by
Darren Lynn Bousman and written by Josh Stolberg and Peter Goldfinger.

12
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
It serves as a spin-off from and the ninth installment of the Saw film series.

13
00:50:22,500 --> 00:50:28,500
The film stars Chris Rock, Max Minghella, Marisol Nichols, and Samuel L.

14
00:54:15,000 --> 00:54:21,000
Jackson, and follows police efforts to stop a Jigsaw copycat killer.

15
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:13,500
The original creators of the series, James Wan and Leigh Whannell, as well as Rock
and series veteran Kevin Greutert, serve as executive producers.

16
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
Talks of another Saw installment began after the release of Jigsaw
(2017), with Rock wanting to branch out into the horror genre.

17
01:05:52,500 --> 01:05:58,500
The project was officially announced in May 2019, with Rock
polishing a script by Stolberg and Goldfinger.

18
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
The rest of the cast joined in July, with filming taking
place in Toronto through that month and August.

19
01:13:37,500 --> 01:13:43,500
Scheduled to be released in May 2020, Spiral was delayed due to the COVID-19 pandemic, and was
theatrically released in the United States on May 14, 2021, by Lionsgate Films.

20
01:17:30,000 --> 01:17:36,000
The film grossed a total of $40.6 million against a budget of $20 million, becoming the lowest
grossing installment in the franchise, and received mixed reviews from critics.

21
01:21:22,500 --> 01:21:28,500
A tenth installment, Saw X, was released in September 2023.

22
01:25:15,000 --> 01:25:21,000
The film explores themes of sequel, murder, police
corruption, survival horror, body count.

23
01:29:07,500 --> 01:29:13,500
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
